1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:02,940
In Core’s left menu, open Deployments.

2
00:00:03,369 --> 00:00:07,050
This workspace keeps a named
assignment, its resources, time

3
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,970
reports and expenses together.

4
00:00:09,329 --> 00:00:13,409
Use it for a community support
assignment, a search operation, a security

5
00:00:13,409 --> 00:00:17,700
detail or a contractor deployment,
as well as fire and E M S work.

6
00:00:18,079 --> 00:00:23,110
The list shows each deployment’s status,
finance mode, identifiers and window.

7
00:00:23,489 --> 00:00:26,649
Select New Deployment to
prepare a separate fictional

8
00:00:26,649 --> 00:00:28,340
community support exercise.

9
00:00:28,559 --> 00:00:30,779
Give the deployment a recognizable Name.

10
00:00:31,279 --> 00:00:33,309
Choose Finance mode deliberately.

11
00:00:33,670 --> 00:00:37,980
The help explains that Operational only
keeps time and expenses for the record,

12
00:00:38,389 --> 00:00:43,410
Cost recovery feeds a reimbursement claim,
and Billable feeds a customer invoice.

13
00:00:43,839 --> 00:00:46,439
This exercise uses Operational only.

14
00:00:46,869 --> 00:00:49,740
Select the fictional
Community Centre as Contact.

15
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:54,480
Call I D is optional; its help
describes one deployment per call.

16
00:00:54,879 --> 00:00:56,480
It stays blank in this example.

17
00:00:56,949 --> 00:01:01,099
Add Notes that explain the assignment
and identify the exercise as fictional.

18
00:01:01,319 --> 00:01:05,160
Set the Window from November second
at eight in the morning to November

19
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,890
fourth at six in the evening.

20
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:12,000
In Jurisdiction, choose the home and host
countries and their state or province.

21
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:14,750
Both are United States, Illinois here.

22
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:17,120
Review Time zone and Currency.

23
00:01:17,509 --> 00:01:21,120
The page explains that the accounting
time zone belongs to the deployment,

24
00:01:21,419 --> 00:01:24,450
while displayed dates and times
use the department’s time zone.

25
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:27,640
This example retains
Central Time and U S D.

26
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:31,669
Out of province or state and
Travel via air remain unchecked

27
00:01:31,669 --> 00:01:33,050
for the local exercise.

28
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:37,150
Use Agency identifiers for the
references supplied for this assignment:

29
00:01:37,509 --> 00:01:42,300
Incident number, Service request
number, Resource order number, Request

30
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:45,050
number, Cost code and Point of hire.

31
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:48,670
The example uses clearly
fictional training references.

32
00:01:49,029 --> 00:01:52,179
These fields help the department
relate its deployment record to the

33
00:01:52,179 --> 00:01:54,179
requesting organization’s paperwork.

34
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:57,509
Select Save, then read
the returned details.

35
00:01:57,870 --> 00:02:02,040
The Saved message and Planned badge
establish that the deployment exists.

36
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:06,150
Verify its window, contact,
jurisdiction and currency

37
00:02:06,179 --> 00:02:07,780
against the intended assignment.

38
00:02:07,949 --> 00:02:10,459
Use Edit to inspect the stored settings.

39
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:13,809
The reopened Window retains
November second at eight

40
00:02:14,030 --> 00:02:15,849
through November fourth at six.

41
00:02:16,209 --> 00:02:17,749
Max days reads three.

42
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:21,800
When an end has not been supplied,
the maximum-days value helps

43
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:25,540
define the deployment window used
for resource checks; this example

44
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:27,229
has an explicit end as well.

45
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:30,629
Check the values before making
a later scheduling change.

46
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:33,249
This visit only verifies what was stored.

47
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:37,549
Use Cancel to return to the deployment
without submitting another edit.

48
00:02:37,719 --> 00:02:41,630
In Roster, choose the training
community van from the unit selector.

49
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:46,589
Enter C S van one as its Call
sign, then select Add unit.

50
00:02:46,959 --> 00:02:49,959
The returned row now lists
that vehicle and call sign.

51
00:02:50,339 --> 00:02:54,540
Its Crew value is initially zero because
no member has been assigned to it yet.

52
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:58,110
Adding a unit and adding its
people are separate steps.

53
00:02:58,509 --> 00:03:01,470
Check the saved unit row before
assigning a member to it.

54
00:03:01,709 --> 00:03:05,640
Under Personnel, choose Matthew
Casey as Member and select the

55
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:07,620
saved community van as Unit.

56
00:03:08,089 --> 00:03:13,060
This training unit has no configured seat,
so Seat and Certification remain blank.

57
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:18,040
Read the seat help: marked seats require
a personnel role, and certification

58
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:20,169
requirements and expirations are checked.

59
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:24,479
Keep Seat even when a requirement
fails unchecked in this exercise.

60
00:03:24,889 --> 00:03:26,280
Select Add member.

61
00:03:26,739 --> 00:03:29,989
Verify that Casey appears beside
the intended unit and that

62
00:03:29,989 --> 00:03:31,559
its Crew count becomes one.

63
00:03:31,979 --> 00:03:35,420
A unit name alone did not establish
that personnel assignment.

64
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:41,559
In Equipment, enter Demo radio kit, select
the same unit and choose Add equipment.

65
00:03:41,969 --> 00:03:44,780
The saved row now associates
the kit with the van.

66
00:03:45,099 --> 00:03:49,139
Its Issued column is a dash in
this exercise: this is a free-text

67
00:03:49,139 --> 00:03:52,739
deployment equipment entry, and
no inventory issue was performed.

68
00:03:53,290 --> 00:03:55,060
Review the final roster together.

69
00:03:55,390 --> 00:03:58,890
It contains the saved unit and
call sign, Casey assigned to

70
00:03:58,890 --> 00:04:00,790
that unit, and the named kit.

71
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:04,110
Use the stored rows to verify
the assignment rather than

72
00:04:04,110 --> 00:04:05,620
relying on a prepared form.

73
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:10,499
Use this same prepare, save and verify
process for community paramedicine

74
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:14,020
and mental health response teams,
search and rescue, security

75
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:18,260
companies, wildland contractors
and industrial emergency teams.

76
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:21,899
Fire and E M S departments
use the same workspace.

77
00:04:22,290 --> 00:04:26,079
Choose names, contacts, unit
assignments and equipment that

78
00:04:26,079 --> 00:04:27,829
fit your organization’s work.

79
00:04:28,239 --> 00:04:31,540
Confirm the people behind the unit
count, and keep the deployment’s

80
00:04:31,569 --> 00:04:35,739
identifiers and window useful for the
supervisors who will review its work.

